---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { YOUTUBE_TERMS_URL } from '../lib/watch/contract';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What Dangerous Robot keeps about you, who can read it, and how to remove it." layout="reading">
  <article class="reading">
    <Breadcrumb crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Privacy' },
    ]} />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      What we keep about you, who can read it, and how to remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading the site</h2>
    <p>
      The site runs no analytics or tracking scripts. The one exception is the <a href="#watch">Watch page</a>, which loads images and video from YouTube. Display settings, such as theme and text size, are saved only in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2 id="watch">Watching videos</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/watch">Watch page</a> shows videos from YouTube, so YouTube (Google) sees your IP address when the page loads. The player loads only when you press Play, and YouTube's own policies then apply. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href={YOUTUBE_TERMS_URL}>YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="petitions">Petitions</h2>
    <p>
      We use your email to confirm your signature, and to send occasional updates about the campaign only if you ask for them. We never show it or share it.
    </p>

    <h3>What we keep when you sign</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name.</li>
      <li>Your email address.</li>
      <li>Whether you want your name shown on the public list of signers.</li>
      <li>Whether you want email updates about the campaign.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your IP address is used for a moment to slow down repeat attempts. It is not saved with your signature.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you start filling in the form, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that a person, not a script, is signing, so the form cannot be used to send email to strangers. Cloudflare sees your IP address during the check. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Who can read it</h3>
    <p>
      Only Dangerous Robot and the petition's authors. Cloudflare stores the list and runs the bot check (Cloudflare Turnstile), Resend delivers the confirmation email, and updates are sent from a petition author's Gmail account, with every address hidden from the other recipients. The public list shows only the names of signers who chose to be listed.
    </p>

    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>If a signature is not confirmed after 4 days, we send a reminder. A signature that is never confirmed is deleted after 7 days.</li>
      <li>When a petition closes, we delete its signers' email addresses. Names and the count stay.</li>
      <li>If you confirmed your signature and asked for updates, we keep your email address after the petition closes, until you ask us to stop.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Stopping updates</h3>
    <p>
      To stop updates, reply to any update or write to <a href="mailto:contact@dangerousrobot.org">contact@dangerousrobot.org</a>. Your signature stays.
    </p>

    <h3>Removing your signature</h3>
    <p>
      Use the removal link in your confirmation email, or write to <a href="mailto:contact@dangerousrobot.org">contact@dangerousrobot.org</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  article h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  article h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
